This mutation changes only `cast_value`. Shields and heals now react to nearby threats and low health. Damage and crowd-control on enemy champions are weighted by how low the target is, and crowd-control gets a bit more value because stun cancels tributes. Camp targeting is unchanged. `goal_field` is left as is, since I couldn't confirm `field_avoid`'s stop semantics well enough to rely on them.

```python
@gene('Z12c', 'value of casting an ability option, threat- and health-aware', parents=['s1'])
def cast_value(o: Option) -> Num:
    k = slot_kind(o.slot)
    hf = me().health_frac
    if k == AB_SHIELD:
        near = count_units(enemies()) > 0 and any(dist(u.pos, me().pos) <= 4 for u in enemies())
        return 88 if hf < 0.7 and near else 0
    if k == AB_HEAL:
        return 85 if hf < 0.6 else 0
    if k == AB_DASH:
        if valid(o.tile) and gems() == 0:
            return 45 if progress(o.tile) >= 2 else 0
        return 0
    if k == AB_CC:
        if exists(o.unit) and o.unit.is_champion and o.unit.is_enemy:
            return 84 + 10 * (1 - o.unit.health_frac)
        if exists(o.unit) and o.unit.is_camp:
            return 58 if gems() == 0 else 0
        return 0
    if k == AB_DAMAGE or k == AB_AOE:
        if exists(o.unit):
            if o.unit.is_champion and o.unit.is_enemy:
                return 76 + 20 * (1 - o.unit.health_frac)
            if o.unit.is_camp:
                return 58 if gems() == 0 else 0
        return 0
    return 0
```

The change makes the bot leave spawn sooner when enemies are close, and it only stays to heal below 95% health. The old rule kept it at spawn until 90%, even mid-fight.

```python
