The change is in `progress` (s4): it returns 0 when either tile is unreachable under the goal field, instead of a huge difference that could make unreachable steps look like progress. `score` (s1) is adjusted only to match the new return convention.

```python
@gene('s4', 'how much closer a step brings me to the goals; 0 when goals are unreachable from either tile', parents=['s4'])
def progress(t: Tile) -> Num:
    d0 = at(GF, me().pos)
    d1 = at(GF, t)
    if d0 > 100000 or d1 > 100000:
        return 0
    return d0 - d1
```

```python
@gene('s1', 'value of doing this option now: heal fully on spawn, focus weak targets, recall at 40%', parents=['s1'])
def score(o: Option) -> Num:
    if o.kind == PICK:
        return pick_value(o.champ)
    if o.kind == BUY:
        return 100 if o.item == 6 else 0
    if o.kind == RECALL:
        if healing():
            return 0
        return 90 if me().health_frac < 0.4 else 0
    if o.kind == ATTACK:
        if o.unit.is_champion:
            return 80 + 10 * (1 - o.unit.health_frac)
        if gems() == 0:
            return 60 + 5 * (1 - o.unit.health_frac)
        return 0
    if o.kind == CAST:
        return cast_value(o)
    if o.kind == TRIBUTE:
        return 70
    if o.kind == MOVE:
